{
  "order": 20000,
  "name": "Tab sessions",
  "kind": "module",
  "responsibility": "What each browser tab owns: its coordinator and voice, and one workhorse for each checkout it works in, found by the thread a notification or tool call names",
  "description": "One record per tab session, opened when a chat socket of the tab connects and built by sessions/factories.ts. The coordinator, voice, spoken approval, coordinator tools and callbacks are the tab's; the workhorses are built on first use, one for each checkout. A notification goes to the session that owns its thread, or to every session when no session owns the thread yet, and a workhorse thread belongs to its workhorse. A tool call from a thread that no session owns is refused, so a running turn never waits on nobody. It notes the conversation shown when each coordinator turn starts and the work each workhorse's operations give. When a session ends, every link is cleared, its approvals are cancelled, its voice and context delivery stop, and its threads are unsubscribed once no turn runs on them.",
